---
// For business — commercial licensing / API / embed enquiries (competitor
// study path 5, closing segment: B9 embed attribution shipped 2026-11-13,
// this page is the enquiry surface). Facts only: counts are computed from
// the data layer at build time, nothing is priced, no customers are named,
// and no update frequency or SLA is promised — arrangements are per enquiry.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import policyChanges from '../data/policy-changes.json';
import { data, verifiedCount, countries } from '../lib/data';

const pairFmt = data.pairCount.toLocaleString('en-US');
const verifiedFmt = verifiedCount.toLocaleString('en-US');
const changeCount = (policyChanges as unknown[]).length;
---

<Base
  title="Visa Requirement Data for Business — Licensing & API Enquiries | visafreely"
  description={`License visafreely's checked visa-requirement dataset (${pairFmt} passport–destination pairs, each checked rule recorded with its official source and date), ask about API access, or embed the free checker widget in your product.`}
>
  <h1>Visa data for your product</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    visafreely keeps a checked record of the entry rules for {pairFmt} passport–destination pairs:
    whether a traveller can enter visa free, on arrival, with an e-Visa or with an ETA, whether a visa
    has to be arranged first, and how long they can stay. If you need those answers inside your own
    product, you can license the dataset or ask us about API access instead of collecting the rules
    yourself.
  </p>

  <h2>What the data covers</h2>
  <ul class="fb-list">
    <li>
      <strong>{pairFmt} pairs</strong> — {countries.length} passports against {countries.length}{' '}
      destinations. Every pair carries one status (visa free, visa on arrival, e-Visa, ETA, visa
      required or no admission) and a maximum stay where the rule sets one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{verifiedFmt} pairs checked against official sources.</strong> Those pairs were checked
      one at a time against a government source, and the check is recorded per pair — the source named
      and the date it was verified. Pairs not yet individually checked carry the dataset value and are
      labelled that way on their pages; see <a href="/about/">how we verify</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>{changeCount} rule changes tracked since March 2025.</strong> When a rule changes, the
      change is written up with its official source on the{' '}
      <a href="/visa-policy-changes/">policy changes page</a>, and the affected route pages are updated
      to match.
    </li>
    <li>
      The same data runs this site's route pages, the <a href="/widget/">embeddable checker</a> and the{' '}
      <a href="/compare/">passport comparison tool</a> — what you see there is the data you would be
      licensing.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Three ways to work with us</h2>
  <div class="fb-cards">
    <section class="fb-card">
      <h3>Dataset licence</h3>
      <p>
        A full copy of the dataset for use in your own systems, under a written licence. How the data
        is kept current after delivery is part of the agreement — tell us how fresh it needs to be for
        your use, and we will only agree to what we can actually deliver.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="fb-card">
      <h3>API access</h3>
      <p>
        If you would rather not hold a copy, we can set up query access by passport and destination.
        Access is arranged per customer rather than self-serve: send a line about what you are building
        and roughly how many lookups you expect, using the form below.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section class="fb-card">
      <h3>Embed the checker</h3>
      <p>
        The <a href="/widget/">checker widget</a> is free to embed, and it stays free. The one
        condition is the attribution inside it — the “Powered by VisaFreely” line and its link must
        stay in place. If you need the checker without attribution, or as part of a product you sell,
        that is a commercial arrangement: ask below.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>

  <h2>What does not change</h2>
  <p>
    The public site. Answers stay free and complete for individual travellers, and every route page
    keeps the official government application route next to any paid option. Licensing is only about
    reuse inside other products — nothing here puts traveller answers behind a paywall.
  </p>
  <p>
    And the warning we give travellers applies under any licence too: this data is a guide, not an
    official source. Requirements change, and the destination's embassy or immigration authority is
    the final word.
  </p>

  <h2>Ask about licensing</h2>
  <p>
    Send a work email and a line about what you are building. There is no price list on this page
    because the arrangements differ — a travel blog embedding the widget, a booking flow checking
    rules at checkout and a relocation firm reusing the whole dataset do not need the same thing. We
    read every enquiry and reply with terms that fit the use.
  </p>

  <form id="fb-form" class="fb-form">
    <div class="fb-field">
      <label for="fb-email">Work email</label>
      <input
        id="fb-email"
        type="email"
        required
        placeholder="you@company.com"
        autocomplete="email"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="fb-field">
      <label for="fb-company">Company <span class="fb-opt">(optional)</span></label>
      <input id="fb-company" type="text" placeholder="Company or site name" autocomplete="organization" />
    </div>
    <div class="fb-field fb-wide">
      <label for="fb-use">What would you use it for? <span class="fb-opt">(optional, one line)</span></label>
      <input
        id="fb-use"
        type="text"
        maxlength="140"
        placeholder="e.g. Booking site — need to show entry rules at checkout"
      />
    </div>
    <div class="fb-actions">
      <button type="submit" class="btn" style="cursor:pointer;">Send enquiry</button>
      <p class="fb-alt">
        Rather write directly? <a href="mailto:partners@visafreely.com">partners@visafreely.com</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <p id="fb-status" hidden></p>
  </form>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var form = document.getElementById('fb-form');
      if (!form) return;
      form.addEventListener('submit', function (e) {
        e.preventDefault();
        var email = document.getElementById('fb-email').value.trim();
        var company = document.getElementById('fb-company').value.trim();
        var use = document.getElementById('fb-use').value.trim();
        var status = document.getElementById('fb-status');
        // The signup service stores {site, email, route} only, so the enquiry
        // detail rides in the route string (kept under its 200-char limit);
        // an enquiry without optional detail lands on the plain page route.
        var route = '/for-business/';
        var parts = [];
        if (company) parts.push('company=' + encodeURIComponent(company));
        if (use) parts.push('use=' + encodeURIComponent(use));
        if (parts.length) route = (route + '?' + parts.join('&')).slice(0, 200);
        fetch('https://honru09--site-stats-web.us-east.modal.run/subscribe', {
          method: 'POST',
          headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
          body: JSON.stringify({ site: 'visafreely', email: email, route: route })
        }).then(function (r) {
          status.hidden = false;
          if (r.ok) {
            status.textContent = 'Thanks — we have your enquiry and will reply by email.';
            form.querySelector('button').disabled = true;
          } else {
            status.textContent = 'That email did not go through — please check it and try again.';
          }
        }).catch(function () {
          status.hidden = false;
          status.textContent = 'Could not reach the enquiry service — please try again later, or write to partners@visafreely.com.';
        });
      });
    })();
  </script>

  <style>
    .fb-list { display: grid; gap: 10px; margin: 0 0 8px; padding-left: 20px; }
    .fb-list li { line-height: 1.55; }
    .fb-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 14px; margin: 14px 0 6px; }
    @media (max-width: 860px) { .fb-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    .fb-card {
      background: var(--card); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: var(--sh-sm);
    }
    .fb-card h3 { margin: 0 0 8px; font-size: 17px; }
    .fb-card p { margin: 0; line-height: 1.55; }
    .fb-form {
      display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px;
      background: var(--soft); border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 18px; margin: 14px 0 8px;
    }
    @media (max-width: 640px) { .fb-form { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
    .fb-field label { display: block; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink-2); margin-bottom: 5px; font-size: 14.5px; }
    .fb-opt { font-weight: 500; color: var(--muted); }
    .fb-field input {
      width: 100%; min-height: 44px; padding: 10px 12px; border-radius: 10px;
      border: 1px solid var(--line-strong); background: #fff; color: var(--ink);
      font: inherit; font-size: 15px;
    }
    .fb-wide { grid-column: 1 / -1; }
    .fb-actions { grid-column: 1 / -1; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
    .fb-actions .btn { min-height: 44px; }
    .fb-alt { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14.5px; }
    #fb-status { grid-column: 1 / -1; margin: 0; color: var(--brand-deep); font-size: 14.5px; }
  </style>
</Base>
